## Summary

Arbitrary values with a `{` that is never closed are accepted and end up in the generated CSS:

```css
.w-\[\{\] {
  width: {;
}
```

The `{` opens a block, so rules that come after it are swallowed. Chromium parses `.w-\[\{\] { width: {; } .underline { text-decoration-line: underline; }` into a single rule, with `.underline` nested inside it.

Nested values like `w-[calc({)]`, `bg-(--a,{)` or `[--a:{]` are accepted too, and a nested `}` like `w-[calc(})]` generates `width: calc(});`.

#20577 rejected unbalanced parens and brackets, but left `{` off the stack so that a top-level `}` (e.g. `[&{color:red}]:flex`) stays invalid. This PR rejects a top-level `{` right away, which keeps that behavior, and tracks nested curlies on the stack so they have to be balanced. Balanced nested curlies like `var(--a,{})` are still allowed.

The Oxide scanner does not extract these candidates, so this affects callers that pass candidates to the JS compiler directly, e.g. `compile().build([…])`.

## Test plan

Added cases to `candidate.test.ts`. They fail without the fix (5 failures), and all pass with it:

```
npx vitest run packages/tailwindcss/src
Test Files  45 passed (45)
     Tests  5543 passed | 1 skipped (5544)
```

`prettier --check` on the changed files and `node scripts/changelog.mjs check` pass.

Output of `build(['w-[{]', 'underline'])`, before:

```css
.w-\[\{\] {
  width: {;
}
.underline {
  text-decoration-line: underline;
}
```

After:

```css
.underline {
  text-decoration-line: underline;
}
```

## Summary

`@tailwindcss/webpack` and `@tailwindcss/turbopack` return a stylesheet unprocessed when `@variant` is the only Tailwind CSS feature it uses:

```css
.btn {
  color: black;
  @variant hover {
    color: red;
  }
}
```

Both loaders output the `@variant hover { … }` block as is. With Turbopack, Next.js then warns `Unknown at rule: @variant`. `@tailwindcss/postcss` turns it into `&:hover { @media (hover: hover) { … } }`.

The loaders skip a file unless its compiler features include `AtApply | JsPluginCompat | ThemeFunction | Utilities`. `Features.Variants` is not in that list. `@tailwindcss/vite` had the same problem and fixed it in #19966. This PR adds `Features.Variants` to both loaders.

## Test plan

- Added `@tailwindcss/webpack loader with only @variant` to `integrations/webpack/loader.test.ts` and `@tailwindcss/turbopack loader with only @variant (dev)` to `integrations/turbopack/loader.test.ts`. Both fail without the fix and pass with it.
- `pnpm vitest --root=./integrations run webpack/ turbopack/`: all tests pass.
- `pnpm vitest run`: all tests pass.
- `pnpm changelog check` and `prettier --check` pass.

